      - uid: root_ssh_accepted
        title: root SSH login accepted on a PVE node
        condition: C
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange:
              from: 900
              to: 0
            datasourceUid: loki
            model:
              datasource:
                type: loki
                uid: loki
              # Inter-node root SSH is constant: pvesr replication and live
              # migration log into each other from the node LAN IPs and the
              # sync/migrate VLANs. Only logins from anywhere ELSE are news.
              expr: 'sum by (host) (count_over_time({job="systemd-journal", host=~"pve0.+"} |~ "Accepted publickey for root" != "COMMAND=" != "from 192.168.86.11" != "from 192.168.86.12" != "from 192.168.86.13" != "from 172.20." != "from 172.21." != "from 127.0.0.1" [10m]))'
              instant: false
              range: true
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: A
              reducer: last
              type: reduce
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: B
          - refId: C
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: "$B > 0"
              type: math
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: C
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        for: 1m
        annotations:
          summary: "root SSH login on {{ '{{' }} $labels.host {{ '}}' }}"
          description: "Root SSH to the PVE nodes is break-glass only (owner's rule: normal access is `amd` + sudo via the forwarded hardware key). This fires on every accepted root key login so a routine-but-wrong habit or a stolen key both become visible. Inter-node root SSH from the node LAN IPs or the sync/migrate VLANs is filtered out of this query, so anything that fires here came from somewhere else."
        labels:
          severity: warning
        isPaused: false
      # cannot distinguish the two (dead container and rejected token are both
      # just up == 0), and this stack has no live HTTP-status probe of the HA
      # API to read a 401/403 from -- roles/victoriametrics templates a
      # blackbox_https_cert job for the HA frontend whose probe_http_status_code
      # would have done it, but that job is NOT deployed on vm-01 (verified
      # 2026-10-21: no blackbox_https_cert targets in /api/v1/targets there).
      # A dead host writes no log line at all, so "this line exists" is a sound
      # proof of life; only an auth rejection can produce it.
      - uid: ha_metrics_scrape_unauthorized
        title: Home Assistant rejected the metrics scrape (auth, not host death)
        condition: C
        data:
          - refId: A
            relativeTimeRange:
              from: 900
              to: 0
            datasourceUid: loki
            model:
              datasource:
                type: loki
                uid: loki
              # homeassistant.components.http.ban logs
              # `Login attempt or request with invalid authentication from <ip>
              #  (<ip>). Requested URL: '<path>'. (<user-agent>)` for any
              # rejected bearer token; the metrics scrape is the only consumer
              # that requests /api/prometheus, so matching on the URL keeps
              # this to the scrape and out of browser login-flow noise.
              expr: 'sum by (host) (count_over_time({job="home-assistant"} |~ "(?i)invalid authentication" [10m]))'
              instant: false
              range: true
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: A
          - refId: B
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: A
              reducer: last
              type: reduce
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: B
          - refId: C
            datasourceUid: __expr__
            model:
              datasource:
                name: Expression
                type: __expr__
                uid: __expr__
              expression: "$B > 0"
              type: math
              intervalMs: 1000
              maxDataPoints: 43200
              refId: C
        noDataState: OK
        execErrState: Alerting
        for: 1m
        annotations:
          summary: "Home Assistant is rejecting the metrics scrape's credentials"
          description: "Home Assistant logged an invalid-authentication request for /api/prometheus in the last 10 minutes, so `up{job=\"homeassistant\"}` is about to go to 0 -- and this is an AUTH failure, not a dead host: HA answered HTTP and wrote this line, so the container is alive. Every rejected request also counts toward HA's IP ban, and once banned the address gets 403 no matter how valid the token is. Fix the credential, not the host: the scrape uses `homeassistant_token` from inventory/group_vars/all.yml (vault) -- check whether that long-lived token still exists on the HA user (HA's 2026-10-18 refresh-token rotation silently deleted three tokens in service), re-mint it if not, and clear any resulting ban (see ha_ip_banned)."
        labels:
          severity: warning
        isPaused: false

      - uid: adguard_dns_down
