          description: "{{ '{{' }} $labels.node {{ '}}' }} has a {{ '{{' }} $labels.kind {{ '}}' }} process for vmid {{ '{{' }} $labels.vmid {{ '}}' }} but its own `pct list` / `qm list` does not manage that guest: a duplicate or split-brain guest. This is exactly what went unseen on 2026-10-21 (a container running on two nodes at once for 22h, and ts-01 running on pve01 while the real one ran on pve02 for 8 days). Do NOT just kill it: `pct stop`/`qm stop` acts on the guest Proxmox knows about, which may be the WRONG copy. Compare `pct list` + `ps -eo args= | grep -E 'lxc-start|/usr/bin/kvm'` on {{ '{{' }} $labels.node {{ '}}' }}, check which copy owns the guest's IPs/MACs (and whether another node still runs it), then stop whichever copy is not backed by the authoritative config. Journal marker from the detector: ORPHAN-GUEST vmid=<n> kind=<ct|vm> node=<node>."
